(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Cellular Automaton to Network by Deconvolution", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"f79799da-420b-4f3d-ba4b-7742168c34d5"],

Cell["Recovering, describing and verifying the generating network", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"efeed03a-a1ec-4a24-bbfc-7a06c5f8a0e3"],

Cell["\<\
An elementary cellular automaton is a synchronous Boolean network: each cell \
is a node connected to its neighbourhood, and the rule is the shared local \
gate. A space-time diagram gives only a trajectory, in which each row is the \
input to the next, not the exhaustive input repertoire. This notebook \
recovers the network from such observations, shows the recovered model in \
full (its connectivity matrix, its gates, and each cell's index-set rule in \
pivot and sumandos form), and compares the original pattern with the \
reconstructed evolution row by row.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d58e504a-a7bb-4658-837b-8030eeb4f26c"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cd750cd7-739d-4540-84d4-dd43a0788e92"],

Cell["\<\
(* Load the forward method, the deconvolution, the cellular-automaton
   deconvolution and the demonstration and detail libraries. *)
nbDir = NotebookDirectory[];
idDir = ParentDirectory[nbDir];
root  = ParentDirectory[idDir];
Get[FileNameJoin[{root, \"papers\", \"method\", \"code\", \"lib\", \
\"CausalBoolCore.wl\"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{idDir, \"src\", \"Deconvolution.wl\"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{idDir, \"src\", \"CADeconvolution.wl\"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{nbDir, \"CADemoLibrary.wl\"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{nbDir, \"CADetailLibrary.wl\"}]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0fd2a8d8-91dc-4a89-b8be-5385929099d5"],

Cell["Walkthrough: rule 90", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"06bcc3ef-cf91-42f9-8ebe-e860b08c0af0"],

Cell["\<\
Rule 90 is the clearest case: its next value is the exclusive-or of the two \
outer cells, so the deconvolution drops the irrelevant centre and names the \
gate XOR over a support of size two.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a08f8f30-3eeb-4c03-9635-1b2f1b2dde1e"],

Cell["\<\
diagrams90 = CAMakeEnsemble[90, 12, 10, 80, 1];
dec90 = DeconvolveCA[diagrams90, 3];
ver90 = VerifyCA[diagrams90, dec90, 90];
Print[\"recovered interior gate     : \", dec90[\"reports\"][[6]][\"canonical\
\"][[1]]];
Print[\"recovered interior support  : \", \
dec90[\"reports\"][[6]][\"support\"]];
Print[\"global map exact            : \", ver90[\"global_map_exact\"]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0bf4d6c0-d732-4fb4-b09c-78eb32387cd7"],

Cell["All example rules", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b45c33bf-a214-45aa-81b0-b6fae7297d4b"],

Cell["\<\
Across the example rules the recovered networks realise the exact global map. \
Rule 254 is recovered as OR, rule 232 as MAJORITY, rule 150 as three-input \
XOR, and the complex rules 30 and 110 as unions of regulatory clauses.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a1d0298-9197-4724-bb92-5be6c5f17f38"],

Cell["allPass = RunCADemo[];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0c646016-3ef6-408b-b41f-7affcdbb6d74"],

Cell["The recovered network (connectivity and gates)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d34a74b6-0ac9-4f02-90ee-8594bf6fe1ca"],

Cell["\<\
The recovered model is defined exactly like the forward model: a connectivity \
matrix C, with C[[k]] listing the cells feeding cell k, and one gate per \
cell. The table lists, for every cell, its gate, its inputs, the size of its \
one-set (the number of global states in which it fires), and the number of \
clauses in its index-set rule.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"428fd7dc-c30c-4efc-91eb-909b8ad38a43"],

Cell["\<\
(* The recovered model is a network: a connectivity matrix and a gate per
   cell.  We take rule 30, one of the most complex, and show the network. *)
diagrams30 = CAMakeEnsemble[30, 12, 10, 80, 1];
dec30 = DeconvolveCA[diagrams30, 3];
Print[\"the recovered network is C (connectivity) plus one gate per cell\"];
Print[\"gates: \", dec30[\"gates\"]];
CBNetworkTable[dec30]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"dc8faedf-d52f-4826-addb-c594e0a9cd30"],

Cell["The index-set rules (pivots and sumandos)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b8241cc8-fd9f-44ee-a464-3b16625aa38f"],

Cell["\<\
Each cell's rule is a short index-set expression: a union of pivot-shifted \
cosets. Each clause has a pivot, the decimal value of its activator cells, \
and ranges freely (the sumandos) over the cells it does not fix. Rule 30 at \
an interior cell is three clauses over its three neighbours; a named gate \
such as XOR is the same structure with a fixed clause pattern.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6f0d7205-cbec-4fa1-924f-fcbc3fe3ce08"],

Cell["\<\
(* Each cell's rule as index-set pivots and sumandos: a union of cosets, one
   pivot (decimal) per clause, shifted over the free cells. *)
CBPrintRule[dec30, 6];
CBPrintRule[dec30, 7];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e3c8e032-b013-4ea1-ae05-d96f64f66fb1"],

Cell["Original versus reconstructed pattern", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c4523ed7-0218-4b8b-8571-8d27a1212858"],

Cell["\<\
The reconstructed network, run forward from the same initial row, reproduces \
the original space-time diagram exactly; the difference panel is entirely \
white.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b4cd23e3-090d-4ee5-b39f-393ca0231920"],

Cell["\<\
(* Original cellular automaton versus the reconstructed network evolution,
   with the difference (all white means identical). *)
cmp30 = CBCompareEvolution[dec30, diagrams30[[1]]];
Print[\"evolution reproduced exactly: \", cmp30[\"match\"]];
Row[{cmp30[\"original\"], cmp30[\"reconstructed\"], cmp30[\"difference\"]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"62605bb2-da6f-48c5-bbd6-10987f65b8ed"],

Cell["Locating a pattern in time", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4b38e0ab-6a80-4693-9110-e2bfe3515483"],

Cell["\<\
Finally we pick a spatial pattern (one row of the diagram) and use the index \
framework to find every time step at which it recurs, highlighting those rows \
in red and reporting their indices.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"750f1a6d-d4f3-4e93-bb91-e103a8f451ba"],

Cell["\<\
(* Locate a chosen spatial pattern in time using the index framework, and
   highlight the matching rows in red with their time indices. *)
hl30 = CBHighlightPattern[diagrams30[[1]], diagrams30[[1, 5]]];
Print[\"target pattern occurs at time steps: \", hl30[\"matching_time_indices\
\"]];
hl30[\"plot\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"126d5e08-71db-40b0-88bf-7ab00cc5401f"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"14.2 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (December 26, 2024)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"ca3303f4-8c5b-415d-b05e-3cf93e78c942"
]
